tal_blocking":0},"body":"### Tested versions\n\n\n4.4 beta2, beta3\nThis works in 4.3\n\n\n### System information\n\n 4.4-beta3 .NET for windows\n\n### Issue description\n\nI use NavigationLink3D for doors. I used tutorial below, but instead of navigation mesh i used NavigationLink3D \n because it works better with Terrain3D https://docs.godotengine.org/en/latest/tutorials/navigation/navigation_different_actor_area_access.html \nMy scene is initialized with NavigationLink3D at layer 2 and when I open door it moves to Layer 1, however NPC still can't calculate path until I modify \"End\" or \"Start\" via \"Remote\" Tab of Scene Tree.\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n1. connect 2 navigation meshes with NavigationLink3D\n2. Set NavigationLink3D layer to 2\n3. Set NavigationAgent3D layer to 1 and NavigationRegion3D layer to 1\n4. Attach script that changes NavigationLink3D layer to 1\n5. At runtime active script to switch NavigationLink3D  layer to 1\nExpected:\nNavigationAgent3D can use NavigationLink3D to reach unreachable navigation mesh\n\nActual:\nNavigationAgent3D doesn't use NavigationLink3D  and can't reach desired mesh\n\n### Minimal reproduction project (MRP)\n\n[pathfindingbug.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/18761829/pathfindingbug.zip)","closed_by":{"login":"Repiteo","id":17489292,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjE3NDg5Mjky","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/17489292?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo","html_url":"https://github.com/Repiteo","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Repiteo/rep